      "message": "fix(docs): make the first 4-axis part model match the round ends of its flats\n\nPR #2135 review: the model had square-ended flats from X-0.875 to\nX-0.125, but the 1/4 in tool cuts each flat in one pass and leaves round\nends, so the model was up to 0.0117 in below the real part there.\n\n- gen_first_4axis_part_obj.py builds the skin as lines along X with the\n  round flat ends; the .obj and the model in the project are regenerated.\n  The posted program is unchanged.\n- the_model_is_the_bar_as_the_program_cuts_it compares the model with\n  the surface the cached toolpaths leave, on a grid over each of the\n  four faces, and at the reviewer's point (X-0.87, 0.05 in off centre).\n- The page and the decision file state the round ends.\n\nRefs #1904\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
